{"author":{"id":"337a442880d7106d509ff84f2f7fef51acce8bce88b081d4f4c3f0298b7e7941"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791663299,"nonce":"YsNSK6ogssdPSZGG+zURk7AaVGw=","message":"Spec 018 revision 3 expands C12. Guard runs on every connection (the console opens one per request) so an old console stops writing once the schema moves. C12 owns the online-backup helper that C6 reuses. Deployment marker \u003cdata_dir\u003e/deployment.toml (mode container, written by C13 preflight): while it exists no command migrates on its own, host or container; a command with pending migrations refuses with run jobhunter upgrade. Exempt commands, which neither migrate nor refuse on pending migrations but still refuse a newer database where they would write: version, paths, secrets status, container preflight, db backup, db restore, upgrade, db migrate. Add jobhunter db migrate (explicit). Without the marker, migration stays automatic, now preceded by a pre-migrate backup. Pre-migrate backups backups/auto/pre-migrate-\u003cfrom\u003e-\u003cto\u003e-\u003cUTC\u003eZ.db keep the newest 3; skipped when the DB is new (version 0). Tests: marker blocks auto-migrate on host and in container mode, restored older-schema DB is not re-migrated, exempt list, per-connection guard after a concurrent migration.","files":null}]}